FALSE(1)                       P32W Unix                        FALSE(1)

NAME
       false - do nothing, unsuccessfully

SYNOPSIS
       false

DESCRIPTION
       false does nothing and exits with status 1. Arguments are
       ignored.

EXAMPLES
       if false; then echo yes; else echo no; fi     prints no

EXIT STATUS
       1.

SEE ALSO
       true(1), sh(1), test(1)
